## 128. storage/cache/.gitkeep - Cache Git Placeholder

**File Location:** `storage/cache/.gitkeep`

**Purpose:** Ensures cache directory exists in Git repository.

```text
# ============================================================
# Cache Directory - Git Placeholder
# ============================================================
# This file ensures the cache directory is tracked by Git.
# The actual cache files are excluded via .gitignore.
# ============================================================

# The cache directory is used by the application to store:
# - Query result cache
# - View compiled templates
# - Route cache
# - API response cache
# - Metadata cache

# This file ensures the directory structure exists
# when cloning the repository.

# Git ignore rules should exclude:
# *.cache
# *.tmp
# *.serialized

# Directory permissions should be:
# - Owner: web server user
# - Group: web server group
# - Permissions: 0755

# For more information, see README.md